e to remain shut in  india  but the government has allowed schools  to call back some of their staff by the  end of this month  for online classes and other related  work however comparative examinations  which take place in the country every  year continue to be conducted  despite protests by students and  petitions to the supreme court for their  postponement  here in uganda's capital kampala schools  remain  closed what you see here is a reflection  of what's happening across the country  right from elementary level  to university level classes remain  closed the government  is not sure of we need to reopen schools  now  especially with the rise in cases of  covet 19.  now many teachers have already lost  their jobs earlier on the government  tried to introduce lessons on radio  and television but sustaining that  became  a challenge so many families have  already described 2020  as a lost academic year  there is no one way of reopening schools  in the u.s  here in washington d.c schools like  francis stevens elementary  remain closed and students continue with  online learning at home  other states happily reopen their  schools but their  kids have to keep their distance from  each other and wear masks all day  that even goes for four and  five-year-olds in kindergarten  one mother has told me that she will  probably not send her daughter to  kindergarten this year because of that  with strict rules like this she says it  feels more like  prison here in beirut the capital of  lebanon  the covet 19 pandemic is not the only  crisis that faces the educational system  right behind me is an exhibit of a  school out of 160 that were totally  destroyed or damaged  due to the colossal beirut port  explosion while the school year  is only a few days away the destruction  that was caused by the shockwaves earth  explosion  aggravated the calamity on residents  already suffering from an unprecedented  economic crisis the german government  is ruling out a second lockdown  